# Earthen Miners Designs

A one-artisan jewelry storefront. The site revolves around a single "current build"
that is forged one piece at a time, then moved into the shop ("The Vault") when done.

Stack: Next.js 16 (App Router), React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind v4, Supabase
(`@supabase/ssr`), Stripe (installed, checkout not yet wired up), `react-easy-crop`.

## Routes

| Route | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `/` | Homepage. Hero scrolls the current build **only when active**. |
| `/shop` | "The Vault" — completed pieces, filter + search. |
| `/workbench` | Live build timeline + video sessions. |
| `/login` | Admin auth portal. |
| `/admin` | Admin hub (guarded by `proxy.ts`). |
| `/admin/current-project` | Manage the live build; finalize it into the shop. |
| `/admin/add-piece` | Manually add a finished piece to the shop. |
| `/admin/homepage` | Editable mirror of `/` — drag, pencil, reorder. |

## The golden rule

The homepage hero animates through `current_build.progress_images` **if and only if**
`current_build.status === 'active'` and it has at least one image. Otherwise show the
standby ("forge resting") state and point the CTA at `/shop`. `/workbench` follows the
same gate.

## The admin owns the storefront

Everything a visitor sees — pieces, photos, categories, reviews, the available
handiworks list, ordering — is editable from `/admin` and read from Supabase.
Never hardcode storefront content in a page component; add it to the database and
an admin editor instead.

Edits must feel **user-intuitive**: mirror the public layout, cyan highlight when
something is movable, pencil on every unit, drag to reorder, click a piece to edit
every stored field. Full ethos: `docs/ADMIN_EDITING.md` and
`.cursor/rules/admin-editing-ethos.mdc`.

## Aesthetic

Industrial-artisan dark theme. Base `#05070A`, panels `#0A0C10`, borders `#27272A`,
teal `#14B8A6`, flash cyan `#00F2FE`, brass `#B59A54`, muted `#71717A`. Oswald for
display text (uppercase, tracked, via `.display-font`), Inter for body. Match this
on any new page.
